{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Keep application data under /srv/data on storage that supports filesystem snapshots.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A dedicated XFS logical volume was created and mounted at /srv/data, populated with application data, and shown as the origin of an active LVM snapshot. The storage and mount recovered successfully after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f3f5f8e9beb14261","cmd-d68d99941fb147d1","cmd-9098dd1cbab346ae","cmd-06d5e8df232c4ff0"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Capture an earlier snapshot, modify the directory, and restore exactly the content captured by that snapshot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline file and whole-tree hashes were captured before the snapshot. Both existing files were changed and a new file added. The snapshot was then merged, and direct comparisons showed identical baseline hashes and content with the added file absent. The restored state remained identical after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9098dd1cbab346ae","cmd-98c3d97d6cee46c3","cmd-3f528721edd248aa","cmd-53451b0c8b9b48c6","cmd-8e2d423408ae4a58","cmd-06d5e8df232c4ff0"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with that platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on CentOS Stream 10 and kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64 before and after execution. The installed LVM, XFS, loop-device, and systemd facilities operated successfully, including across reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d3c56f54ef664bdc","cmd-f3f5f8e9beb14261","cmd-d68d99941fb147d1","cmd-06d5e8df232c4ff0","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.91,"summary":"The implementation left no failed services, new network exposure, or damaged package state. The only clearly unnecessary mutation was creating /mnt/srv-data-check for an unsuccessful troubleshooting mount; no removal was captured, so the empty directory apparently remained (cmd-dbcf38bd040c4804). Five small checksum files used for bounded verification also remained in /tmp rather than being cleaned up; they were created by cmd-8e2d423408ae4a58, cmd-1f4cc6d93e054756, and cmd-06d5e8df232c4ff0. Other mutations had clear roles in provisioning snapshot storage, demonstrating rollback, correcting the transient mount problem, or performing the required restart protocol.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dbcf38bd040c4804","cmd-8e2d423408ae4a58","cmd-1f4cc6d93e054756","cmd-06d5e8df232c4ff0","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence of the complete snapshot transition: healthy baseline, snapshot creation, divergent modifications, merge-based rollback, exact hash/content recovery, and persistence after reboot. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: it records healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and connection interruption, a changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle observations, and recovered services, mount, storage, and identical data.","limitations":["The fixed lifecycle snapshots independently corroborate the reboot and unchanged platform but do not inventory /srv/data or LVM state; those outcomes rely on the detailed executor command captures.","The lifecycle temporary-file inventory does not cover /mnt, so retention of the troubleshooting directory is inferred from its creation and the absence of a captured removal."]}
